  "rationale": "The batch shows a repeated possessive noun-phrase pattern: after a proper noun and 's, an adjective can follow. The representative prefix Mia + 's gives the target small only 0.0031 probability, while red and apples dominate; the existing small root lacks a possessive-context rule, although red has one. Add a modest rule for small after any visible possessive marker, without conditioning on the name. The stories also repeatedly place ate after a comma and a proper-noun subject, and place the after lowercase and in an introductory noun phrase; modest suffix rules support those observed contexts. These are contextual biases, not hard constraints: possessives can be followed directly by nouns or other modifiers, comma-final proper nouns can precede verbs other than ate, and conjunctions can introduce other phrases. The batch contains varied openings and endings, so no single framing or continuation is asserted.",
